  "solution": {
    "text": "Parabolas <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> touch each other at the line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;(<math><mo>∵</mo></math> both parabolas are inverse of each other)<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is the common tangent at <math><mi>P</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> we get point <math><mi>P</mi></math> by solving <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> point of contact <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
